                "file": "src/Lending.Application/UseCases.fs",
                "line": 10,
                "quote": "query ports (Views.searchAt text (BranchId branchId))"
              }
            ],
            "rationale": "No new effects. searchAt uses the existing Store port through `query`. The Tier 2 and Tier 3 additions are pure. The CLI change only dispatches and formats (the ' at {branch}' suffix).",
            "score": 2
          },
          "ARC-REV-03": {
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Application/Views.fs",
                "line": 61,
                "quote": "List.filter (fun copy -> copy.Book = bookId)"
              },
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Transition/Catalog.fs",
                "line": 136,
                "quote": "search text library |> List.filter (fun book -> shelved.Contains book.Id)"
              }
            ],
            "rationale": "The ISBN match and the branch-existence check have one definition each, and searchAt reuses search and findBranch. The fact 'copy c of book b is shelved at branch x' is stated twice: in Catalog.searchAt and again in Views.searchAt. The two agree, but they are separate predicates that could drift apart.",
